# ngx_http_heavybag_module - INTENTIONALLY EMPTY UA signature list (test fixture)
#
# Zero patterns, on purpose. Consumed by:
#   - heavybag-protocol-test.conf "uamerge" vhost (28509) / run-protocol-tests.sh
#     Part C: a child level that points a waf_*_list at this file OWNS that
#     category slot and turns it OFF -- it must NOT re-inherit the parent's
#     compiled regex (ua-list-01 / T5.c). C8 there also asserts the
#     "loaded 0 UA pattern(s)" NOTICE, which only a real start emits.
#
# run-config-tests.sh V35 covers the config-time twin (an explicitly empty
# waf_bot_list must LOAD, not abort) against its own generated $WORK copy, so
# that harness stays self-contained in its generated corpus.
#
# Every line here is a comment or blank, so ngx_http_heavybag_ua_list_compile
# pushes zero tokens and compile_bucket leaves ua_re[cat] == NULL. That NULL is
# exactly why the merge sentinel had to move from the compiled regex to the
# list PATH (ua_list[cat].data): the regex alone cannot distinguish
# "not configured at this level" from "configured to match nothing".
#
# DO NOT add a pattern to this file -- its emptiness IS the fixture.
